<title>GERMANY: Bonn sells 10.3 bln dmk Bubills at 98.49 and above.</title>
<headline>Bonn sells 10.3 bln dmk Bubills at 98.49 and above.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government on Wednesday sold 10.306 billion marks of 6-month zero-coupon Treasury Bills, or Bubills, at an auction at a lowest accepted price of 98.49 and for an average yield of 3.00 percent, the Bundesbank as fiscal agent said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The weighted average price was 98.506 percent.</p>
<p>Banks bids totalled 19.586 billion marks, the Bundesbank said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
